                <pb facs="0496" n="1330" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 659.119/354</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grant-Smith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-29T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.57 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2452. Delegates of Central Powers will begin negotiations with Danish
                    associations July 8, in Copenhagen, for new four months’ arrangement for the
                    exchange of products. Iron and steel manufactures important articles for which
                    Germany will receive compensation. Is War Trade Board prepared to license
                    immediately 1,500 <pb facs="0497" n="1331" xml:id="pg1331"/> to 2,000 tons of
                    wrought iron tubing for prompt shipment to weaken enemy’s position in
                    negotiations? Indication on our part to raise embargo on iron and steel products
                    will not alone serve to reduce quantities which Germany will receive in
                    compensation but will tend to reduce prices demanded. Urgent. Copy to
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grant-Smith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
